+
+### MPPI Humble simulation experiment
+
+`tools/navigation_evaluation/mppi_humble_experiment/` contains a pinned Nav2
+1.1.20 patch, not a replacement for the default navigation profile. It adds a
+collision-scored rotation-only arrival domain and reapplies constraints after
+Humble's Savitzky-Golay filter. The separate relaxed patch adds a coupled
+mecanum wheel projection before sampled trajectory scoring and after sequence
+filtering. The model geometry is explicitly configured; it is not a physical
+calibration result.
+
+Use `make build-mppi-experiment MPPI_EXPERIMENT_WS=/absolute/external/workspace`
+inside the ROS Humble environment. `make test-mppi-experiment` runs the optimizer
+and smoke suites. The workspace must be external to source and its pinned
+upstream/patch provenance must match; choose a new directory for a different
+patch. `MPPI_EXPERIMENT_PATCH` selects the separate relaxed patch. See the
+experiment README for configuration and evidence boundaries. None of these
+settings are automatically loaded by the common runtime. Simulation-only
+external safety bypass requires the recorded experiment runner and is never a
+physical robot configuration.
